description:
Two production-path unwrap/expect sites to address:

1. install.rs:249 — `results.into_iter().next().unwrap()` after an is_empty() guard. Safe but violates err-no-unwrap-prod. Replace with:
   ```rust
   let Some(first) = results.into_iter().next() else { unreachable!() };
   ```
   Or refactor to return the first element directly from the search function.

2. file_edit.rs:33 — `.expect("language_info required for LanguageWithPackages")` panics on a logic error. Currently safe because build_install_plan always sets language_info when mode is LanguageWithPackages, but the type system doesn't enforce this. Consider a LanguageInstallPlan newtype or restructure InsertionMode to carry the LanguageInfo directly:
   ```rust
   enum InsertionMode {
       LanguageWithPackages(LanguageInfo),
       // ...
   }
   ```

source.rs:254-283: score_match uses 13 unlabeled numeric thresholds (0.3, 0.45, 0.52, 0.60, 0.65, 0.68, 0.75, 0.80, 0.82, 0.85, 0.95, 0.98, 1.0) that encode a scoring hierarchy but are hard to reason about.

Extract to named constants:
```rust
const EXACT_ROOT_PNAME: f64 = 1.0;
const EXACT_ROOT_TAIL: f64 = 0.98;
const EXACT_NESTED_PNAME: f64 = 0.85;
// ... etc
const MIN_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD: f64 = 0.3;
```

Also document the scoring intent: why is pname > tail? Why 0.98 vs 0.95? This would help when tuning scores later.

InstallPlan has three boolean fields (is_brew, is_cask, is_mas) at plan.rs:39-43 that are derived from source_result.source at construction time. This duplicates state—tests construct InstallPlan manually and could desync these booleans from the source.

After PackageSource becomes an enum (sibling issue), replace these with methods:
```rust
impl InstallPlan {
    fn is_brew(&self) -> bool { matches!(self.source_result.source, PackageSource::Homebrew) }
    // etc.
}
```

Or just match on the source directly at the 3 usage sites in ai_engine.rs:build_edit_prompt.

Files: domain/plan.rs, infra/ai_engine.rs (build_edit_prompt)
